      "widgets_values": [
        "Convert the entire scene of <ref_image_0> into a loose hand-painted ink-and-watercolor illustration matching the painting technique of <ref_image_1>. Use the first image only for the arrangement and recognizable silhouettes of the blue teapot, white cup, table and left window. Use the second image for the visual medium across every surface. The teapot body is painted as broad transparent ultramarine pigment pools with irregular wet edges and cream-paper gaps; thin broken black ink strokes trace its cylindrical outline, lid, spout and handle. The cup is a simplified white paper shape with a few diluted gray brush marks. The tabletop consists of broad ochre brush strokes rather than detailed wood grain. The window and wall become loose pale green and gray washes. Rough cream watercolor paper grain is visible through the subjects and the background, and soft violet paint forms the shadows. The whole frame reads as a drawing on paper with visibly simplified painted forms."
      ]
